   "html_text": "The same type of nonidentity problem arises but at a more local level in Kavka’s slave child case. In exchange for $50,000, a couple enters into a binding contract according to which the couple will conceive and bear a child who will be transferred at birth to a wealthy man as a slave (Kavka 1982, 100). The child is conceived and born pursuant to the contract – and, as a slave, suffers but still has a life worth living. We think what the couple has done is “outrageous” (Kavka 1982, 101). And at ",
